## 8. Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------------|
| Regional font rendering inconsistency across devices | Use web-safe Noto Sans family with preload, provide font subset bundles |
| Large image uploads fail on slow networks | Implement TUS resumable uploads (already supported), add chunked upload UI |
| WhatsApp OG image not displaying correctly | Test 1200x630px format across WhatsApp versions, use static fallback |
| Calendar import failures on different platforms | Extensive testing on Google Calendar, Apple Calendar, Outlook; RFC 5545 strict compliance |
| Auto-deletion timing issues across timezones | Use UTC internally, convert to Asia/Kolkata only for display and scheduling |
| Rate limiting affects legitimate high-traffic events | Implement graduated limits, allow burst for authenticated users |

---

## 9. Architecture Clarification Required

**CRITICAL DECISION NEEDED**: The feature request specifies **Laravel 11 (PHP 8.3)** and **Next.js with React 18** as the technology stack. However:

1. **All RawDrive microservices use Python/FastAPI** (gallery-service, billing-service, upload-service, notifications-service, ai-service, etc.)
2. **An invitations-service already exists** at port 8007 with Python/FastAPI
3. **Frontend is React 18 + Vite**, not Next.js
4. **The existing service has substantial functionality** already implemented

**Options:**
1. **Enhance existing Python/FastAPI service** (Recommended) - Maintains architectural consistency
2. **Create new Laravel service on different port** - Adds complexity, requires inter-service communication
3. **Replace existing service with Laravel** - Significant rewrite, loses existing work

---
